The dzil build against Alien::libssh 0.003 (share build, libssh 0.12.2) warns at LibSSH.xs:636:

  warning: ssh_channel_get_exit_status is deprecated [-Wdeprecated-declarations]

libssh 0.11.0 deprecated ssh_channel_get_exit_status() in favour of ssh_channel_get_exit_state(channel, &exit_code, &exit_signal, &core_dumped). In 0.12.2 the old function is a thin wrapper: it calls get_exit_state(channel, &code, NULL, NULL) and returns SSH_ERROR (-1) for any rc != SSH_OK, SSH_AGAIN included. So the behaviour today is fine; the risk is a future libssh removing the old symbol.

A plain swap is not possible: Alien::libssh accepts a system libssh >= 0.9.0 (alienfile minimum_version), and ssh_channel_get_exit_state only exists since 0.11.0 (symbol version node LIBSSH_4_10_0, alongside sftp_home_directory and ssh_channel_request_pty_size_modes, which the libssh CHANGELOG lists as new in 0.11.0).

Done when:
- exit_status() calls ssh_channel_get_exit_state under #if LIBSSH_VERSION_INT >= SSH_VERSION_INT(0,11,0), and the old call stays as the #else branch
- every rc other than SSH_OK still yields -1 (POD contract: -1 until the remote process has exited), signal/core_dumped passed as NULL, no new leak
- dzil build compiles without the deprecation warning; dzil test is green with the integration suite actually running (not skip_all)
- no new API (an exit_signal method would be a separate card)

